{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nFour `graph` functions carry moderate cyclomatic complexity in the checked-in ratchet (`.github/complexity-baseline.json`), re-measured on this base and unchanged: `_blockers.py::_find_direct_blockers` (18), `_graph.py::_get_all_blocked_by` (20), `_graph.py::check_cycle_at_level` (16), `_unblock.py::detect_newly_unblocked` (22). LOW-RISK: pure logic, `graph.*` is in the mypy strictness ratchet, extensive existing tests, zero in-progress contention. The high-risk orchestrators `next_batch.compute` (CCN 42) and `import_ndjson.import_tickets` (CCN 45) are deliberately EXCLUDED. Flagged by audit ae1b.\n\n## Root cause (architectural)\n`graph/_loader.py` is a 15-line shim that stops at raw `reduce_ticket`/`reduce_all_tickets`, so higher-level query logic is hand-rolled per call-site. TWO distinct patterns recur and drive the CCN:\n1. The **exact** \"reduce_all → drop `error`/`fsck_needed` → index by id\" loop is duplicated verbatim in `_find_direct_blockers` (`_blockers.py:33-40`) and `_compute_dep_graph` (`_graph.py:65-72`) — identical policy (`reduce_all_tickets(exclude_archived=False, exclude_session_logs=True)` + drop error/fsck).\n2. `_get_all_blocked_by` (`_graph.py:127`) and `check_cycle_at_level` (`_graph.py:223`) each re-implement an FS-walking BFS skeleton (queue/visited + per-node `reduce_ticket` + try/except + dep-scan).\n\n## Approach (conservative, behavior-preserving — reconcile divergent node-sets, do NOT unify them)\nAdd exactly two shared helpers and refactor onto them WITHOUT changing any function's node-set or traversal results:\n\n1. `graph/_loader.py`: add `load_indexed_states(tracker_dir) -> dict[str, dict]` reproducing pattern (1) EXACTLY (`reduce_all_tickets(exclude_archived=False, exclude_session_logs=True)` via the `reducer` module attribute so the existing `_loader_module.reducer.reduce_all_tickets` patch point still works, then drop `error`/`fsck_needed`, index by `ticket_id`). Apply it at ONLY the two identical-policy sites: `_blockers.py:33-40` and `_graph.py:65-72`.\n\n2. `graph/_relations.py` (already hosts `build_blocked_by`): add a shared **accumulator** BFS skeleton, `bfs(starts, neighbors_fn) -> set[str]`, where `neighbors_fn(node, visited) -> Iterable[str]`. **Contract (stated explicitly because the two call-sites' outputs differ structurally):**\n   - `bfs` owns ONLY queue/visited bookkeeping: pop, skip if visited, mark visited, call `neighbors_fn`, add every yielded id to an **accumulator** set and enqueue it when not already visited. All I/O, reduce calls, exception-swallowing and filtering stay in each `neighbors_fn`; `bfs` has no policy.\n   - The returned set is the **accumulator**, NOT `visited`: a start node is absent unless a real edge yields it, and a yielded id is present even when no ticket dir backs it (never dequeued). That is exactly `_get_all_blocked_by`'s `blocked` set (`_graph.py:151` adds every `blocks` target before any existence check). A `visited`-returning bfs would wrongly include the seed and break `check_would_create_cycle`'s `target_id in _get_all_blocked_by(source_id)` test.\n   - `visited` is passed to `neighbors_fn` (read-only) because both loops consult it when deciding what to yield (`_graph.py:160-161`, `:266`); without it the accumulator would differ.\n   - `_get_all_blocked_by` becomes `return bfs([ticket_id], neighbors)`, `neighbors` reproducing its per-node behavior verbatim (dir-exists → `reduce_ticket` → yield `blocks` targets unconditionally; then `os.listdir` → skip visited/hidden/non-dirs → `reduce_ticket` → yield entries whose `depends_on` targets `current`).\n   - `check_cycle_at_level` becomes `return source_id in bfs([target_id], neighbors)` after its existing `not level` / self-loop early returns. Its mid-loop `if current == source_id: return True` is equivalent: the seed cannot be `source_id` (self-loop already returned), so `source_id` is dequeued iff some `neighbors_fn` yielded it, iff it is in the accumulator. Dropping the early return changes only how far the walk goes, never the boolean; the walk is bounded by the level-filtered dep component reachable from `target_id`, not by tracker size, and no perf test covers this function.\n   - Both keep raw `reduce_ticket` (NO error/fsck filter, NO session-log exclusion) — NOT routed through `load_indexed_states`, so their node-set is unchanged.\n\n3. `_find_direct_blockers`: use `load_indexed_states` for the load branch; extract the two blocking sources named in its own docstring into `_own_depends_on_blockers` / `_blocks_targeting` helpers to cut branching.\n\n4. `detect_newly_unblocked`: extract its inline scandir+tombstone loader (`_unblock.py:53-80`) into a named module-level helper `_load_states_with_tombstones` (kept in `_unblock.py`; NOT merged with `load_indexed_states` — its tombstone semantics differ); keep the readiness logic and the existing `build_blocked_by` reuse.\n\nExplicitly OUT OF SCOPE / untouched (divergent semantics, per reviewer): `_ready.py` (documented dependency-light — must NOT import the heavy `_loader`), `_status.py::_get_ticket_status` (a status *predicate* mapping error→closed, not a loader), and `_unblock.py::batch_close_operations`.\n\nRationale (G6): centralizing only the provably-identical loop (site 1) plus one accumulator-BFS skeleton lowers CCN and removes the growth-driving duplication, while leaving each function's node-set/traversal identical — so the change is behavior-preserving and the next graph query has a loader/bfs to reuse instead of hand-rolling a fifth copy.\n\n## Scope\n- `src/rebar/graph/_loader.py` — add `load_indexed_states`.\n- `src/rebar/graph/_relations.py` — add accumulator `bfs` helper.\n- `src/rebar/graph/_blockers.py` — `_find_direct_blockers` on `load_indexed_states` + two source-helpers.\n- `src/rebar/graph/_graph.py` — `_compute_dep_graph` uses `load_indexed_states`; `_get_all_blocked_by` + `check_cycle_at_level` on `bfs` with behavior-identical `neighbors_fn`.\n- `src/rebar/graph/_unblock.py` — extract `_load_states_with_tombstones`; `detect_newly_unblocked` uses it.\n- `tests/scripts/graph/test_graph_cycles.py` — ADD one characterization test (below).\n- `.github/complexity-baseline.json` — regenerate (`python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --update-stale`), shrink-only.\n\n## Verification (behavior-preserving refactor)\n- **The behavioral oracle is the whole `tests/scripts/graph/` directory (notably `test_graph_cycles.py`, `test_graph_traversal.py`, `test_graph_unresolved_blocker.py`, `test_graph_perf.py`) plus `tests/scripts/test_ticket_unblock.py`** — the suites that actually import the four functions. They pass UNCHANGED (no edits to existing tests).\n- **One NEW characterization test** is required because no existing test pins the accumulator-vs-visited distinction: assert `_get_all_blocked_by` still returns a `blocks` target whose ticket dir does NOT exist (unconditional add), and that the seed id is absent from the result. Write it RED-first against `origin/main` (it must pass there, proving it characterizes current behavior) before the refactor.\n- Complexity gate green with the four ceilings regenerated downward; `mypy src/rebar/graph` + `make lint` green.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `.github/complexity-baseline.json` records `_find_direct_blockers` ≤ 8, `_get_all_blocked_by` ≤ 8, `check_cycle_at_level` ≤ 8, `detect_newly_unblocked` ≤ 12 (verified: `python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check` exits 0).\n- [ ] The inline \"reduce_all → drop error/fsck → index\" loop is gone from `_find_direct_blockers` and `_compute_dep_graph`; both call `load_indexed_states` (verified by reading the two functions).\n- [ ] `_ready.py`, `_status.py::_get_ticket_status`, and `_unblock.py::batch_close_operations` are unchanged (verified: `git diff origin/main` touches none of those three symbols).\n- [ ] `_get_all_blocked_by` and `check_cycle_at_level` return results identical to origin/main (verified: `tests/scripts/graph/` and `tests/scripts/test_ticket_unblock.py` pass with no edits to existing tests).\n- [ ] The new characterization test asserts `_get_all_blocked_by` includes a `blocks` target with no backing ticket dir and excludes the seed id (verified: it passes on origin/main AND after the refactor).\n- [ ] `mypy src/rebar/graph` is green.\n- [ ] `make lint` is green."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786597669393800001,"uuid":"905afec1-056c-44cd-9442-a3a45dc77eb3"}